An earlier review of this plan reported findings, and the author revised the plan in response. candidate_plan is the revision. findings holds one entry per earlier finding: finding is that finding as the author received it, and values_at_location holds the plan values at the place its location names. values_at_location.plan_path is that location read as a field path inside candidate_plan; reviewed_value is the value at that path in the plan you reviewed before, and current_value is the value at the same path in candidate_plan. Each value is {"state": "value", "value": <the value at that path>}, or {"state": "absent"} when that plan has no value at that path. When a location is not one field path that exists in either plan, values_at_location is {"state": "location_not_resolved"} and holds no values; read candidate_plan for that finding yourself. values_at_location_example shows the form for an example finding. author_response lists the top-level plan fields the revision changed and the values those fields held in the plan you reviewed before.
